## Context

Child of 0817. The author ruled that rung 3 is not called "acceptance"
(2026-09-23): acceptance is his own use. The driver is still
`bench/sitter_acceptance.py` and its records sit in `verification/acceptance/`.
Mechanical, no behaviour change, and first, so 0821, 0822 and 0818 build on the
new names instead of colliding with the rename.

## Actions

1. `git mv` the driver to a rung name (e.g. `bench/sitter_menagerie_rung.py`)
   and the record directory to match; keep the committed records' history.
2. Sweep every reference in one commit: `bench/`, `tests/`, `Makefile`,
   `plugins/sdt-sitter/TESTING.md`, `STATE.md`, and the **whole** `tickets/`
   tree — not only this raid's tickets. Open ticket 0793 names the driver and
   its `build_record()` shape; 0815 and 0818 name the record directory.
3. Leave `DECISIONS.md` and closed tickets as written (append-only history).

## Test

A guard or test that fails while any live file outside the append-only set
still names the old path; shown red before the sweep.

## Exit criteria

No live reference to the old names; `make check` green; the moved records
still resolve from `TESTING.md`.
